  "result": "All 7 tests pass (4 existing plus the 3 new ones in tests/test_t2.py).\n\n**Changes in `editor/buffer.py`:**\n\n- **Generalized the command object.** The internal command now stores `old` and `new` text at a position instead of an insert/delete flag. Apply swaps old for new, invert swaps back. Insert is the case where old is empty, delete is where new is empty, and replace has both.\n- **Added `replace(pos, n, s)`.** It validates the range the same way delete does and records one command holding both the removed and inserted text, so it undoes and redoes as a single step.\n- **Added `history_len()`.** Returns the length of the undo stack.\n- **Added `undo_all()`.** Calls undo until it returns False. Each undone step lands on the redo stack, so everything stays redoable.\n\nNo files under `tests/` were touched. Nothing is committed yet.",
